WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.320 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  Brianna Taylor would have been 27 years  old on June 5th had she not been killed  in her own home  when Louisville police officers made a  late night raid on the wrong address  looking for someone who had been taken  into police custody hours earlier she  was shot eight times and no arrests have  been made now some of the biggest stars  in Hollywood are paying tribute to  Brianna on what would have been her 27th  birthday cardi B took to Twitter writing  that Brianna's story is so sad and  unfair adding the fight ain't over til  you get justice Selena Gomez pointed  that she and Brianna would have been the  same age before urging her followers on  Twitter to sign a petition demanding  that charges be filed against the  officers involved Emmy Rossum Sara  Bareilles Kerry Washington niecy Nash  Jeffrey star and Ellen DeGeneres also  tweeted their support on Taylor's  birthday for those of you at home  looking for ways to pay tribute to  Brianna Taylor here's how number one say  her name continue to say Brianna  Taylor's name whether that's protesting  in the street or on social media and on  Friday  use the hashtag say her name and  birthday for Brianna to share tributes  artwork and calls to action number two  send a letter join in the birthday card  Drive mailing letters to the Attorney  General and the Louisville Metro mayor  at these addresses demanding the  officers responsible for Taylor's death  get charged you can also email the  Attorney General and Mayor number three  sign a petition the easiest way to lend  your voice is to sign the justice for  Brianna Taylor petition which in part  calls for charges to be filed and the  arrests of the officers involved  immediately you can also text enough to  five five one five six number four  donate you can donate directly to  Brianna's family through a verified  GoFundMe and you can also donate to the  Louisville community bail fund which  serves protestors on the ground in  Louisville as they fight for justice for  Taylor and to bring an end to police  brutality and systemic racism  [Music]

